==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*ad}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂éd||near, at}}. Cognates include {{cog|en|at|}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Preposition===
{{la-prep|accusative}}

# {{lb|la|direction}} [[toward]], [[to]]
#* {{Q|la|Lucretius|De rerum natura|4|quote=Fugere '''ad''' puppim collēs campīque videntur.|trans=The hills and fields appear to fly '''toward''' the ship.}}
#* {{Q|la|Pliny the Elder|Naturalis Historia|2|quote=Meridie umbrae cadunt '''ad''' septentrionem, ortu vero '''ad''' occasum.|trans=At noon the shadows fall '''towards''' the north, [and] at sunrise, point '''to''' the west.}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|93|quote=Duplices tendens '''ad''' sidera palmas.|trans=Stretching both hands '''to''' the stars.}}
# [[up to]] {{q|indicating direction upwards}}
# [[near]], [[by]], [[close by]], [[at]], [[to]] {{q|indicating location}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]], [[w:ab urbe condita libri|ab urbe condita]], I, 33|quote='''ad''' {{l|la|Murcia|Murciae}} {{l|la|datae}} {{l|la|sedes}}|t=the residences being given near the Murcia}}
# [[against]], [[on]], [[upon]] {{q|indicating position}}
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Gallico|6|27|quote=Sē '''ad''' arborēs applicant.|trans=They are leaning '''against''' the trees.}}
# [[at]], [[about]], [[around]], [[on]], [[in]]  {{q|indicating a point in time}}
# [[until]], [[to]], [[up to]], [[till]] {{q|indicating the extent of time}}
# [[for]], [[to]], [[toward]] {{q|indicating purpose or aim}}
#: {{ux|la|'''Ad''' maiōrem Deī glōriam.|t='''For''' the greater glory of God.}}
# [[in order to]], [[to]], [[for]] {{q|indicating means}}
#: {{ux|la|'''Ad''' vim atque '''ad''' arma confugere.|t=To resort '''to''' violence and '''to''' fighting.}}
# in [[comparison]] with, in [[comparison]] to, in [[relation]] to
# [[according to]] {{q|indicating conformity}}
# in [[consequence]] of
# [[against]], [[at]] {{q|indicating movement 'toward' but in a hostile manner}}
# [[among]], [[amongst]] {{q|indicating the sharing of a characteristic}}

====Usage notes====
* The word '''ad''' is an [[antithesis]] to {{m|la|ab}} (just as {{m|la|in}} is to {{m|la|ex}}; in a progressive order of relation, {{m|la|ad}} denotes, first, the direction toward an object; then the reaching of or attaining to it; and finally, the being at or near it.)
* Often used of geographical position of a place in reference to the points of compass, with the verbs {{m|la|iaceō||lie, be situated}}, {{m|la|vergō||incline, slope}}, {{m|la|spectō||observe, see}} etc.:
*: ''Asia iacet '''ad''' meridiem et austrum, Europa '''ad''' septentriones et aquilonem.''
*:: Asia lies '''near''' the prime meridian and the south, Europe '''near''' the northern regions and northern wind. (There are two words for north.)
*: '''''Ad''' Atticam vergente.''
*:: Inclining '''to''' Attic.
* When appended to the beginning of a word beginning with a consonant, ''ad-'' often assimilates, e.g. becoming ''ap-''  in {{m|la|appretiō}}, from {{m|la|pretium}}, or ''ac-'' in {{mention|la|accedo|accēdō}}, from {{mention|la|cedo|cēdō}}. Note that unassimilated forms such as {{m|la|adpretiō}} are also found.

